<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch inflation seen steady at 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch inflation seen steady at 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch consumer price inflation for August is expected to be steady at a year-on-year rate of 2.1 percent, according to a Reuter poll of bank economists.</p>
<p>The August inflation data are due on Friday morning.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator    Consensus  Range    Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  13/9  August   CPI yr/yr    2.1 pct    2.0-2.3  2.1</p>
<p> 0830  13/9  August   CPI mth/mth  0.2 pct    0.1-0.3  0.3</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, IRIS, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
